{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774719,"nonce":"rm2Yb0/gCLQYY+VCMncrDGLVe4E=","title":"refactor(server): resolve run governance once via a typed RunGovernance","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #35 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `refactor/run-governance` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-18T20:08:21Z · Merged: 2026-07-18T20:08:35Z\n\n\nThe pipeline `environment:` reference was unpacked from `Option\u003cString\u003e` at several admission/persistence sites in `admit_and_create_run` / `persist_run_from_ir`, each re-deriving a *different* consequence — protection rules, deploy-ness, fork lockout, deploy context, grant policy — with its own `Some`/`None` handling.\n\nThis resolves it **once** into a typed value:\n\n```rust\nenum RunGovernance {\n    Ungoverned,\n    Governed { environment: String, locked_out: bool, protection: Option\u003cProtectionRules\u003e },\n}\n```\n\n- The **variant** is the deploy-vs-CI discriminator: targeting an Environment makes a run a deploy (opts out of newest-wins auto-cancel, records a deploy context).\n- The nested **`protection: Option\u003c_\u003e`** is whether that Environment is actually *defined*.\n\nKeeping those two axes distinct is deliberate and **preserves existing behavior**: deploy-ness keys on the *reference* (`ir.environment.is_some()`), while ref/grant enforcement keys on the *resolved rules* (`protection.is_some()`). A referenced-but-undefined environment therefore stays a deploy that is permissive on refs and fail-closed on governed grants — exactly as before.\n\nCall sites now read as intent (`gov.protection()`, `matches!(gov, Ungoverned)`, `if let Governed { environment, .. }`); `persist_run_from_ir` sheds two params (`protection`, `locked_out`) for one `\u0026RunGovernance`.\n\n\nThis is the \"simplify without inventing an entity\" alternative to adding a default/implicit environment — no new persisted row, no ownership/lifecycle questions, no risk of a permissive default opening privileged escalation. `Ungoverned` is still the *absence* of governance, just spelled as a type.\n\n\n- **No behavior change.** `admit_step_grants` and the inline `create_run` path are untouched.\n- One file, internal only (`crates/scarab-server/src/lib.rs`).\n\n\n- `just check` — clean\n- `cargo test -p scarab-server -p scarab-project` — **171 passed, 1 ignored** (environments / dispatch / trigger / allowed_refs / secret_injection / placement suites all green)\n- clippy on the new code — clean\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}